## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates a candidate's ability to design concrete, layered security controls for a common integration risk in SaaS platforms. It tests understanding of both transport-layer and application-layer protections.

## Key Concepts
- Webhook signature verification using HMAC
- Replay protection via timestamps and narrow validation windows
- Secret management and rotation policies
- Transport security with mutual TLS (mTLS)

## Code Example
```javascript
const crypto = require('crypto');

function verifyWebhookSignature(payload, secret, signature, timestamp, windowMs = 300000) {
  const now = Date.now();
  if (now - timestamp > windowMs) return false;
  const data = \`${timestamp}.${payload}\`;
  const expected = crypto.createHmac('sha256', secret).update(data).digest('hex');
  return crypto.timingSafeEqual(Buffer.from(signature), Buffer.from(expected));
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design scalable supply chain and third-party risk controls for real-time data platforms, including attestation, signing, SBOM management, and incident response coordination with external vendors.

## Key Concepts
- Supply chain security and third-party risk management
- Artifact signing with Sigstore/cosign and SBOM generation
- Per-artifact IAM and ephemeral credentials via AWS STS
- Runtime attestation for serverless and container environments
- Incident response playbooks, containment strategies, and vendor communications

## Code Example
```javascript
// Verify artifact signature and SBOM integrity before deployment
async function verifyArtifact(artifactUrl, sbomUrl, expectedDigest) {
  const artifact = await fetch(artifactUrl);
  const artifactDigest = await computeSHA256(artifact);

  if (artifactDigest !== expectedDigest) {
    throw new Error('Artifact integrity check failed');
  }

  const signature = await cosign.verify(artifact, publicKey);
  const sbom = await spdx.parse(fetch(sbomUrl));
  const components = sbom.getVulnerableDependencies();

  return { signature, components, isTrusted: signature.valid };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical application of confidential computing to multi-tenant isolation in real-time ML workloads, beyond token-based controls.

## Key Concepts
- Confidential computing (TDX/Nitro/SEV)
- Per-tenant attested enclaves and key management
- Envelope encryption of in-flight data and outputs
- Attestation-based admission control at API gateway
- IR playbook with measurable success criteria

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-spec showing attestation flow
function attestedInference(req, enclave) {
  if (!enclave.attest(req.tenant)) throw new Error('Untrusted tenant');
  const input = enclave.declassify(req.input, req.tenant);
  const out = enclave.infer(input);
  return enclave.envelope(out, req.tenant);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rotate per-tenant keys without service downtime?
- How would you detect and respond to a compromised enclave?
